  "term": "calcium-channel blocker",
  "definition": "A calcium-channel blocker is a drug class that includes nicardipine. In the source, nicardipine is described as being widely used to lower blood pressure in severe hypertension after events such as ischemic stroke, traumatic brain injury, and intracerebral hemorrhage.",
